{"requirements":[{"id":"logical-volume-mounted","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted read-write at /srv/data on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"vg_data/lv_data was created, formatted as ext4, and mounted read-write at /srv/data. The final post-restart observation confirms the LV remained active and mounted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9d9b83ab72b343b2","cmd-c7a5f4f531584f81"]},{"id":"online-growth-and-integrity","requirement":"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while it remains mounted and preserve its existing contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The LV grew online from 1 GiB to 2,147,483,648 bytes. resize2fs explicitly detected the mounted filesystem, the mount source was unchanged before and after growth, and checksums created before growth passed afterward and after the final restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-63cdd46e8bb64c89","cmd-b3f94347eaa046d3","cmd-c7a5f4f531584f81"]},{"id":"retain-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged from baseline through the final recovered state. The installed LVM, loop, systemd, and ext4 tooling operated successfully on that platform.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-e1cf200c2abe4144","cmd-c7a5f4f531584f81","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Storage creation and persistence configuration directly supported the required LV and the mandatory restart validation (cmd-700d32938d074f01, cmd-9d9b83ab72b343b2, cmd-51db69c31d42435a). The two interim boot defects were diagnosed and corrected by cmd-3fe6ed6c3eb04e8f and cmd-161bbfd920704aab; the final restart showed a healthy system with no failed units. Temporary reboot artifacts were absent from the final bounded /tmp inventory, package health remained sound, and no new unsafe listening service appeared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-700d32938d074f01","cmd-9d9b83ab72b343b2","cmd-51db69c31d42435a","cmd-3fe6ed6c3eb04e8f","cmd-161bbfd920704aab","cmd-c7a5f4f531584f81","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct evidence shows creation and mounting of the LV, online growth to 2 GiB with checksum-preserved contents, and retention of the original OS and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered writable storage, data, services, and node health. The final boot identity also agrees with the fixed after-executor observation.","limitations":[]}
